AWSTemplateFormatVersion: "2010-09-09"

Description: >-
  Vocareum AWS lab Bedrock reachability probe. Answers one question: can this
  student account call an Amazon Bedrock foundation model, and if not,
  exactly why. It creates nothing persistent.

  A Lambda-backed custom resource runs four probes at create time and CATCHES
  every error, so the stack reaches CREATE_COMPLETE and reports the diagnosis
  as Outputs. A generic AccessDenied rollback tells you nothing, which is the
  situation this template exists to escape. Read the Verdict, NextAction and
  Reason outputs first.

  Deploy by uploading this file to /voc/private/lab.template in Configure
  Workspace. The filename must be exactly lab.template, so keep the real
  lab.template elsewhere while this probe is in place.

# The four probes, in order:
#   1. sts:GetCallerIdentity          Which principal was actually tested.
#   2. bedrock:ListFoundationModels   Control plane. Is Bedrock reachable at
#      all. Needs no per-account model access grant, so it cleanly separates
#      "Bedrock is blocked" from "this model is not invokable".
#   3. Converse via the US geographic inference profile. The normal path.
#   4. Converse via the bare in-Region model ID, only if probe 3 failed. That
#      path does no cross-Region routing, so a pass here after a failure at 3
#      points at a Region-scoped org policy rather than at Bedrock itself.
#
# Assumptions and known blind spots:
#   - The probe runs as the Lambda execution role, NOT as the student's
#     vocareum/sysNNNNNNN role. Service control policies apply to every
#     principal in the account, so an SCP_DENY verdict is conclusive for the
#     student too. A pass is NOT conclusive: it proves the org ceiling allows
#     Bedrock, not that the student's own role holds the IAM permission. That
#     second question is answered by lab.policy.
#   - Creating the Lambda function and its IAM role is itself unverified
#     against the ceiling. If the stack fails on ProbeFunctionRole or
#     ProbeFunction, the ceiling blocks IAM or Lambda and the Bedrock question
#     is still unanswered. Set ExecutionRoleArn to an existing role to drop
#     the iam:CreateRole dependency, then try again.
#   - No AWS::Logs::LogGroup is declared on purpose. Lambda creates its log
#     group lazily, so a logs deny costs you the logs but still returns the
#     verdict. Declaring the group would let a logs deny fail the whole stack.

Parameters:
  ModelId:
    Type: String
    Default: anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0
    Description: >-
      Bare foundation model ID for Claude Haiku 4.5, used by the in-Region
      fallback probe. Confirmed against the Bedrock model card at
      docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-anthropic-claude-haiku-4-5.html
      Haiku is the cheapest current Anthropic model on Bedrock and the probe
      caps output at 8 tokens, so a full run costs a fraction of a cent
      against the $100 per month student budget.

  InferenceProfileId:
    Type: String
    Default: us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0
    Description: >-
      US geographic cross-Region inference profile ID for the same model.
      This is the primary probe target. Claude Haiku 4.5 supports In-Region
      invocation in us-east-1 but NOT in us-west-2, so the bare model ID
      alone would raise a ValidationException in us-west-2 that looks like a
      permissions failure. The us. profile works from both AgentCore regions.

  ExecutionRoleArn:
    Type: String
    Default: ""
    Description: >-
      Optional ARN of an existing role for the probe function to assume.
      Leave empty and the template creates a least-privilege role. Set it to
      an existing role, for example the LabRole that Vocareum-hosted accounts
      commonly provide, if the ceiling denies iam:CreateRole. The role must
      trust lambda.amazonaws.com.

Conditions:
  # Only build an IAM role when the caller did not supply one. This is the
  # single knob that lets the probe be retried without iam:CreateRole.
  CreateExecutionRole: !Equals [!Ref ExecutionRoleArn, ""]

Resources:
  ProbeFunctionRole:
    Type: AWS::IAM::Role
    Condition: CreateExecutionRole
    Properties:
      AssumeRolePolicyDocument:
        Version: "2012-10-17"
        Statement:
          - Effect: Allow
            Principal:
              Service: lambda.amazonaws.com
            Action: sts:AssumeRole
      Policies:
        - PolicyName: bedrock-probe
          PolicyDocument:
            Version: "2012-10-17"
            Statement:
              # Control plane probe. bedrock:ListFoundationModels is a
              # Region-wide list operation and does not support
              # resource-level permissions, so "*" is the only valid value.
              # It reads model metadata only and grants no inference.
              - Sid: ListModelsControlPlane
                Effect: Allow
                Action: bedrock:ListFoundationModels
                Resource: "*"

              # Primary invoke probe. Scoped to the one inference profile
              # this template names, in this Region and account only.
              - Sid: InvokeViaInferenceProfile
                Effect: Allow
                Action: bedrock:InvokeModel
                Resource: !Sub >-
                  arn:${AWS::Partition}:bedrock:${AWS::Region}:${AWS::AccountId}:inference-profile/${InferenceProfileId}

              # A geographic inference profile also needs the foundation
              # model itself allowed in every destination Region it routes
              # to. The Region wildcard is bounded two ways: to this one
              # model, and by the InferenceProfileArn condition to requests
              # arriving through the profile above. That is tighter than
              # hardcoding the destination list and stays correct if AWS adds
              # a destination Region to the US profile.
              - Sid: InvokeModelBehindThatProfile
                Effect: Allow
                Action: bedrock:InvokeModel
                Resource: !Sub >-
                  arn:${AWS::Partition}:bedrock:*::foundation-model/${ModelId}
                Condition:
                  ArnEquals:
                    bedrock:InferenceProfileArn: !Sub >-
                      arn:${AWS::Partition}:bedrock:${AWS::Region}:${AWS::AccountId}:inference-profile/${InferenceProfileId}

              # Fallback probe. The bare model ID in this Region only, with
              # no inference profile involved, so it can still be reached
              # when cross-Region routing is what is blocked.
              - Sid: InvokeModelInRegionDirect
                Effect: Allow
                Action: bedrock:InvokeModel
                Resource: !Sub >-
                  arn:${AWS::Partition}:bedrock:${AWS::Region}::foundation-model/${ModelId}

              # CloudWatch Logs, so a truncated Output can be chased in the
              # log stream. The function name is generated by CloudFormation
              # and is unknowable at authoring time, so the group name is
              # wildcarded within this account's Lambda log groups.
              - Sid: WriteOwnLogs
                Effect: Allow
                Action:
                  - logs:CreateLogGroup
                  - logs:CreateLogStream
                  - logs:PutLogEvents
                Resource: !Sub >-
                  arn:${AWS::Partition}:logs:${AWS::Region}:${AWS::AccountId}:log-group:/aws/lambda/*
      Tags:
        - Key: Purpose
          Value: vocareum-bedrock-probe
        - Key: StackName
          Value: !Ref AWS::StackName

  ProbeFunction:
    Type: AWS::Lambda::Function
    Properties:
      # No FunctionName is set, so CloudFormation generates one. A fixed name
      # would collide if a previous lab session failed to delete its stack,
      # and Vocareum resets labs often.
      Runtime: python3.13
      Handler: index.handler
      Role: !If
        - CreateExecutionRole
        - !GetAtt ProbeFunctionRole.Arn
        - !Ref ExecutionRoleArn
      # 60s is well clear of four short API calls. A Lambda that times out
      # sends no response at all and leaves the stack hanging for an hour.
      Timeout: 60
      MemorySize: 256
      # Inline ZipFile only. The Vocareum flow has no build or upload step,
      # so an S3 artifact could never be staged.
      Code:
        ZipFile: |
          """Probe Amazon Bedrock from inside the student account.

          Every probe is caught and classified. The handler always reports
          SUCCESS to CloudFormation and puts the diagnosis in the response
          data, so the stack completes and the verdict is readable as a
          stack Output instead of a rollback message.
          """

          import json
          from typing import Any

          import boto3
          import cfnresponse
          from botocore.config import Config
          from botocore.exceptions import BotoCoreError, ClientError

          # Short timeouts and few retries. The stack must never wait on a
          # hung socket, because a Lambda timeout means no response is sent
          # and CloudFormation sits in CREATE_IN_PROGRESS for an hour.
          BOTO_CONFIG = Config(
              connect_timeout=5,
              read_timeout=20,
              retries={"max_attempts": 2, "mode": "standard"},
          )

          # A custom resource response body is capped at 4096 bytes in
          # total, so every field is truncated before it goes in.
          MAX_DETAIL = 250
          MAX_REASON = 600

          PROMPT = "Reply with the single word ok."

          NEXT_ACTION = {
              "SCP_DENY": (
                  "A service control policy in Vocareum's AWS Organization "
                  "blocks this. Nothing in lab.template or lab.policy can "
                  "raise it. Send Vocareum support the policy ID printed in "
                  "the Reason output."
              ),
              "RCP_DENY": (
                  "A resource control policy in the Organization blocks "
                  "this. Same escalation path as an SCP: only Vocareum can "
                  "change it."
              ),
              "IAM_DENY": (
                  "The calling role lacks the action. This is fixable "
                  "inside the account, in lab.policy or in the probe role. "
                  "No Vocareum involvement needed."
              ),
              "MODEL_ACCESS_NOT_GRANTED": (
                  "Bedrock is reachable but model access was never granted "
                  "for this model in this Region. Grant it on the Model "
                  "access page of the Bedrock console. This is an account "
                  "setting, not a policy problem."
              ),
              "MODEL_LEGACY_INACTIVE": (
                  "Authorization passed, but the provider marked this model "
                  "legacy and this account did not use it during the activity "
                  "window. Choose an active model from ListFoundationModels."
              ),
              "MODEL_USE_CASE_NOT_SUBMITTED": (
                  "Authorization passed, but Anthropic use-case details are "
                  "not active for this account or destination Region. Submit "
                  "the provider form and retry after it propagates."
              ),
              "MODEL_ID_INVALID": (
                  "The model ID or inference profile ID is not valid for "
                  "this Region. This is a template value problem, not a "
                  "permissions problem. Check the model card."
              ),
              "MODEL_NOT_IN_REGION": (
                  "The model is not offered in this Region. Use the us. "
                  "inference profile or move the lab to us-east-1."
              ),
              "REACHABLE_THROTTLED": (
                  "The call was authorized and then throttled, so access "
                  "works. Retry, or raise the account quota."
              ),
              "REACHABLE_QUOTA": (
                  "The call was authorized and then hit a service quota, "
                  "so access works. Request a quota increase."
              ),
              "ENDPOINT_UNREACHABLE": (
                  "The Bedrock endpoint could not be reached from Lambda. "
                  "Suspect a network or endpoint problem, not a policy."
              ),
              "OK": "No action needed.",
          }


          def _clip(text: str, limit: int) -> str:
              """Trim text to limit characters, marking any truncation."""
              text = " ".join(str(text).split())
              if len(text) <= limit:
                  return text
              return text[: limit - 3] + "..."


          def classify(error: ClientError) -> tuple[str, str]:
              """Map a botocore ClientError onto a verdict and a message."""
              info = error.response.get("Error", {})
              code = info.get("Code", "Unknown")
              message = info.get("Message", str(error))
              lowered = message.lower()

              if code == "AccessDeniedException":
                  # AWS names the blocking policy type in the message body.
                  # That string is the only reliable way to tell an
                  # org-level ceiling apart from a gap in the account's own
                  # IAM, and both arrive as AccessDeniedException.
                  if "service control policy" in lowered:
                      return "SCP_DENY", message
                  if "resource control policy" in lowered:
                      return "RCP_DENY", message
                  # This exact phrase is IAM's authorization failure. It
                  # never appears in Bedrock's model-access wording, so
                  # testing it before the model-access phrase is safe.
                  if "not authorized to perform" in lowered:
                      return "IAM_DENY", message
                  # Bedrock's wording when the model exists and the caller
                  # is authorized, but access was never granted for this
                  # account in this Region.
                  if "access to the model" in lowered:
                      return "MODEL_ACCESS_NOT_GRANTED", message
                  return "ACCESS_DENIED_UNCLASSIFIED", message

              if code == "ResourceNotFoundException" and (
                  "marked by provider as legacy" in lowered
                  or ("legacy" in lowered and "last 30 days" in lowered)
              ):
                  return "MODEL_LEGACY_INACTIVE", message
              if (
                  code == "ResourceNotFoundException"
                  and "use case details" in lowered
              ):
                  return "MODEL_USE_CASE_NOT_SUBMITTED", message

              mapped = {
                  "ValidationException": "MODEL_ID_INVALID",
                  "ResourceNotFoundException": "MODEL_NOT_IN_REGION",
                  "ThrottlingException": "REACHABLE_THROTTLED",
                  "ServiceQuotaExceededException": "REACHABLE_QUOTA",
                  "UnrecognizedClientException": "CREDENTIALS_BROKEN",
                  "InvalidSignatureException": "CREDENTIALS_BROKEN",
              }
              return mapped.get(code, code.upper()), message


          def probe_identity(region: str) -> dict[str, str]:
              """Report which principal the probes actually run as."""
              client = boto3.client("sts", region_name=region,
                                    config=BOTO_CONFIG)
              try:
                  who = client.get_caller_identity()
              except ClientError as error:
                  status, message = classify(error)
                  return {"status": status, "detail": message}
              except BotoCoreError as error:
                  return {"status": "ENDPOINT_UNREACHABLE",
                          "detail": str(error)}
              return {"status": "OK", "detail": who["Arn"]}


          def probe_list_models(region: str) -> dict[str, str]:
              """Call the Bedrock control plane. No model grant required."""
              client = boto3.client("bedrock", region_name=region,
                                    config=BOTO_CONFIG)
              try:
                  models = client.list_foundation_models(
                      byProvider="anthropic"
                  )["modelSummaries"]
              except ClientError as error:
                  status, message = classify(error)
                  return {"status": status, "detail": message}
              except BotoCoreError as error:
                  return {"status": "ENDPOINT_UNREACHABLE",
                          "detail": str(error)}
              return {
                  "status": "OK",
                  "detail": (
                      f"{len(models)} Anthropic models visible in {region}"
                  ),
              }


          def probe_invoke(region: str, model_ref: str) -> dict[str, str]:
              """Invoke a model through Converse and report the outcome.

              Converse maps to the same bedrock:InvokeModel IAM action as
              InvokeModel but needs no anthropic_version in the body, which
              removes a way to raise a ValidationException that would look
              like a permissions failure.
              """
              client = boto3.client("bedrock-runtime", region_name=region,
                                    config=BOTO_CONFIG)
              try:
                  response = client.converse(
                      modelId=model_ref,
                      messages=[
                          {"role": "user",
                           "content": [{"text": PROMPT}]}
                      ],
                      inferenceConfig={"maxTokens": 8, "temperature": 0},
                  )
              except ClientError as error:
                  status, message = classify(error)
                  return {"status": status, "detail": message}
              except BotoCoreError as error:
                  return {"status": "ENDPOINT_UNREACHABLE",
                          "detail": str(error)}

              usage = response.get("usage", {})
              return {
                  "status": "OK",
                  "detail": (
                      f"{model_ref} answered, "
                      f"{usage.get('totalTokens', 0)} tokens"
                  ),
              }


          def run_probes(
              region: str, model_id: str, profile_id: str
          ) -> dict[str, str]:
              """Run every probe and fold the results into one verdict."""
              identity = probe_identity(region)
              control = probe_list_models(region)
              profile = probe_invoke(region, profile_id)

              # Only pay for the second invoke when the first one failed.
              # The bare model ID does no cross-Region routing, so a pass
              # here after a profile failure isolates a Region-scoped org
              # policy rather than Bedrock being blocked outright.
              if profile["status"] == "OK":
                  direct = {
                      "status": "SKIPPED",
                      "detail": "Inference profile already worked.",
                  }
              else:
                  direct = probe_invoke(region, model_id)

              if profile["status"] == "OK":
                  verdict, cause = "BEDROCK_OK", profile
              elif direct["status"] == "OK":
                  verdict, cause = "BEDROCK_OK_IN_REGION_ONLY", profile
              elif control["status"] == "OK":
                  verdict, cause = "BEDROCK_REACHABLE_MODEL_BLOCKED", profile
              else:
                  verdict, cause = "BEDROCK_BLOCKED", control

              action = NEXT_ACTION.get(
                  cause["status"],
                  "Unclassified failure. Read the Reason output and the "
                  "function log stream.",
              )
              if verdict == "BEDROCK_OK_IN_REGION_ONLY":
                  action = (
                      "The bare model ID works but the US inference profile "
                      "does not, so cross-Region routing is what is "
                      "blocked. Check for a Region-restricting SCP: the US "
                      "profile routes to us-east-1, us-east-2 and "
                      "us-west-2, and blocking any one of them breaks it."
                  )

              return {
                  "Verdict": verdict,
                  "Reason": _clip(cause["detail"], MAX_REASON),
                  "NextAction": _clip(action, MAX_REASON),
                  "ProbedPrincipal": _clip(identity["detail"], MAX_DETAIL),
                  "ControlPlaneStatus": control["status"],
                  "ControlPlaneDetail": _clip(control["detail"], MAX_DETAIL),
                  "InferenceProfileStatus": profile["status"],
                  "InferenceProfileDetail": _clip(profile["detail"],
                                                  MAX_DETAIL),
                  "DirectModelStatus": direct["status"],
                  "DirectModelDetail": _clip(direct["detail"], MAX_DETAIL),
              }


          def handler(event: dict[str, Any], context: Any) -> None:
              """Run the probes and always answer CloudFormation."""
              print(json.dumps({"RequestType": event.get("RequestType")}))
              data: dict[str, str] = {}
              try:
                  if event.get("RequestType") == "Delete":
                      cfnresponse.send(
                          event, context, cfnresponse.SUCCESS, {},
                          physicalResourceId="bedrock-probe",
                      )
                      return
                  props = event.get("ResourceProperties", {})
                  data = run_probes(
                      region=props["Region"],
                      model_id=props["ModelId"],
                      profile_id=props["InferenceProfileId"],
                  )
                  print(json.dumps(data))
              except Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001
                  # Deliberate catch-all, and the one place a broad except
                  # is correct here. Anything escaping this frame would
                  # leave CloudFormation waiting an hour for a response
                  # that never arrives, which is the exact failure mode
                  # this template exists to avoid.
                  data = {
                      "Verdict": "PROBE_ERROR",
                      "Reason": _clip(
                          f"{type(error).__name__}: {error}", MAX_REASON
                      ),
                      "NextAction": (
                          "The probe itself failed before it could reach "
                          "Bedrock. Read the function log stream."
                      ),
                  }
              cfnresponse.send(
                  event, context, cfnresponse.SUCCESS, data,
                  physicalResourceId="bedrock-probe",
              )
      Tags:
        - Key: Purpose
          Value: vocareum-bedrock-probe
        - Key: StackName
          Value: !Ref AWS::StackName

  BedrockProbe:
    Type: AWS::CloudFormation::CustomResource
    Properties:
      ServiceToken: !GetAtt ProbeFunction.Arn
      # Passed as properties rather than read from the environment so that a
      # stack update with a different model ID re-runs the probe.
      Region: !Ref AWS::Region
      ModelId: !Ref ModelId
      InferenceProfileId: !Ref InferenceProfileId

Outputs:
  Verdict:
    Description: >-
      One of BEDROCK_OK, BEDROCK_OK_IN_REGION_ONLY,
      BEDROCK_REACHABLE_MODEL_BLOCKED, BEDROCK_BLOCKED, PROBE_ERROR
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.Verdict

  NextAction:
    Description: What to do about the verdict, and who has to do it
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.NextAction

  Reason:
    Description: >-
      Raw AWS error message behind the verdict. An SCP deny names the
      offending policy ID here, which is what Vocareum support will ask for.
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.Reason

  ControlPlaneStatus:
    Description: >-
      bedrock:ListFoundationModels result. OK means Bedrock is reachable in
      this account and Region regardless of any model access grant.
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.ControlPlaneStatus

  ControlPlaneDetail:
    Description: Count of visible Anthropic models, or the error message
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.ControlPlaneDetail

  InferenceProfileStatus:
    Description: >-
      Converse result through the US geographic inference profile, the
      InferenceProfileId parameter. This is the primary probe.
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.InferenceProfileStatus

  InferenceProfileDetail:
    Description: Token usage on success, or the classified error
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.InferenceProfileDetail

  DirectModelStatus:
    Description: >-
      Converse result through the bare in-Region model ID. SKIPPED when the
      inference profile already worked.
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.DirectModelStatus

  DirectModelDetail:
    Description: Token usage on success, or the classified error
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.DirectModelDetail

  ProbedPrincipal:
    Description: >-
      The role the probes ran as. This is the Lambda execution role, not the
      student's vocareum role. An SCP deny applies to every principal in the
      account and is conclusive. A pass proves the org ceiling allows
      Bedrock, not that the student's own role is permitted.
    Value: !GetAtt BedrockProbe.ProbedPrincipal

  LogsLink:
    Description: CloudWatch log group for the probe function
    Value: !Sub https://${AWS::Region}.console.aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/home?region=${AWS::Region}#logsV2:log-groups/log-group/$252Faws$252Flambda$252F${ProbeFunction}
